// Moving-platform testbed — the map tapes/platform_ride.tape runs against.
//
// Two ledges with a spiked pit between them, and one platform ferrying across.
// The pit is lethal on purpose: `expect no died` is then a real assertion that
// the ride worked, rather than a statement that falling in was survivable.
//
// A new file rather than an addition to testbed_platform.ron, which is frozen —
// its tapes encode its exact pixels. Treat this one as a fixture too.
//
// Legend: '#' solid  '^' spikes  'P' spawn.  Moving platforms have no grid
// character: a character can say where something is but not where it goes, so
// they are authored as `Platform(...)` entries below.
//
// 24x12 tiles at 32px = 768x384 world pixels.
//
//   spawn        col 2, row 7      world (70, 222), feet on the ledge at y=256
//   left ledge   cols 0-4          surface y=256, x 0..160
//   right ledge  cols 19-23        surface y=256, x 608..768
//   pit          cols 5-18         spikes at y 336..352, x 160..608
//   platform     3 tiles solid, top y=256 — level with both ledges, so it is
//                walked onto and off rather than jumped between.
//                from (5, 8) = x 160, docked against the left ledge
//                to   (16, 8) = x 512, right edge 608, flush with the right
//                88 px/s over 352px = 240 ticks a leg, 480 ticks a round trip.
//                phase 420 puts it back at the left ledge on tick 60, which is
//                after the player has walked to the edge and stopped — the
//                whole point being that the ride is boarded, not jumped onto.
Level(
    tileset: "castle",
    grid: [
        "########################",
        "#......................#",
        "#......................#",
        "#......................#",
        "#......................#",
        "#......................#",
        "#......................#",
        "#.P....................#",
        "#####..............#####",
        "#####..............#####",
        "#####^^^^^^^^^^^^^^#####",
        "########################",
    ],
    entities: [
        Platform(from: (5, 8), to: (16, 8), tiles: 3, speed: 88.0, phase: 420),
    ],
)
